      "id": "ba034527-6a92-4324-a133-7ba069fb11b4",
      "title": "Original opening (Talmud anecdote)",
      "content": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "An earlier draft began with the Talmud, in which every page is a small piece of architecture: a central column of Mishnah, a band of Gemara around it, Rashi's commentary on the inner margin, and the Tosafot on the outer. Reading is a vertical act and a lateral act at the same time. The page literally cannot be read in linear order. Cut for length, but worth coming back to."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "createdAt": "2026-04-23T14:00:00.000Z",
